==Strategy==
Use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to rush the starting enemies of the stage, as they are weak. One hit from A. Bahamut and Maglev is enough to kill the starting weak enemies. If you do not have either of them, then it is a sure sign that you are not ready for this stage. This stage should be treated like a merciless stage, or a very difficult deadly stage.

[[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blocker Cats]] (excluding [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]) help to protect longer ranged units such as [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] and [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] from [[Wave Attack]]s caused by Crazed Titan Cat.

Since the enemies spawn on timer, it is possible to rush down the base before the bigger threats of the stage appear. Use some starting money combos, as said above, you can kill crazed cow using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to get double money, use rusher units such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and hope to kill the first few enemies before Crazed Cat arrives. Since the latter one has a slow movement speed, [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Cannon]] can be used to push him behind the base opening the path for A. Bahamut and your other units to destroy the base before Crazed Axe arrives. If owned, [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] can also weaken the enemies making A. Bahamut survive for longer.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST Exclusives]]: Any Epicfest exclusive can make this stage much more manageable because of their high stats and debuffs against traitless.
*[[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]]: The crazed cats push very hard, so having cats with great survivability and knockbacks is recommend, which is where Shishilan Pasalan shines with his 100 knockbacks. Thanks to his crippling berserker DPS and Wave Immunity, Shishilan Pasalan is a great help in this stage. Crazed Lizard may be a nuisance to him though, since they could interrupt his attacks with how easily he gets knocked back.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: The boss killer is an obvious choice for a stage of all bosses. Lufalan Pasalan's high ranged DPS works great here, as he can outrange all but Crazed Lizard, allowing him to pick off the threats one by one. Naturally, since Crazed Lizard Cat will stay in the back, Lufalan Pasalan can stay safe by targeting the frontliners.
*Good [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] Ubers: Long Distance units such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]] or [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] are useful for sniping certain Crazed Cats that hide behind others, such as the Crazed Lizard or Crazed Titan.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: This generally underestimated Uber is very good for all crazed cat stages, as it's low cost, fast cooldown, amazing dps and high ranged omnistrike allow it to quickly kill most of the enemies in this stage.

